## stdlib/fs.zag — Phase 2 read_file smoke-test example.
##
## Reads a small known file and prints its byte count. The exact
## file is `examples/basics/hello.zag` — a tiny source file with
## predictable content (assert its size are stable across zag
## revisions so the smoke run's expected-output pin holds).
##
## Heap-ownership contract (Phase 2 v1 limitation): the returned
## `[]u8` is `page_allocator`-owned. We don't `free()` here because
## the v1 `.free_expr` overload only handles pointer-shaped slots
## via `std.heap.page_allocator.destroy(ptr)`. A v1 smoke run that
## exits immediately after printing leaks one page (4 KiB) which
## the OS reclaims on process exit — acceptable for the
## smoke-test scope. A future Phase 2.1 widening will add
## `free <slice-expr>` to `.free_expr` so this example can
## close over with `defer free data`.

import std.fs.{read_file};

fun main() {
    let data = read_file("examples/basics/hello.zag");
    print("read {data.len} bytes\n");
}
